# Design Principles

## Zero Trust Security
Trust no user or device by default and continuously validate access.

## Verify Explicitly
Use identity, device, location, and risk signals before granting access.

## Least Privilege Access
Provide only the minimum permissions required.

## Risk-Based Access Control
Make access decisions based on risk levels and threat intelligence.

## Continuous Access Evaluation
Continuously monitor and reassess access permissions throughout user sessions.

## Outcome
Conditional Access strengthens Zero Trust identity security and secure resource access.